{"call_id":"8d4b804b7b84ea0e","request_hash":"31fbdb0f2c5067068a526aab7858a5e15d62827a7f0ae05624858442b3e18ff6","model_label":"gemini-3.8-flash","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"SHARED-000","condition":"gemini-3-8-flash"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"31fbdb0f2c5067068a526aab7858a5e15d62827a7f0ae05624858442b3e18ff6","provider":"google","model_requested":"gemini-3.8-flash","model_returned":"gemini-3.8-flash","text":"If your Halvard Home Keel washing machine vibrates more than usual, take the following steps:\n\n* Pause the programme and wait for the drum to stop before checking the machine [P1].\n* If the door unlocks, distribute heavy items (such as towels) evenly around the drum, and then restart the programme [P1]. Do not force the door open [P1].\n* Check that the machine sits firmly on a hard, level floor; ensure all four feet touch the floor and that the machine does not rock when gently pushed at opposite corners [P1].\n* If the machine is newly installed, check the installation guide to verify that the transit bolts have been removed [P1].\n* Stop using the machine and contact Halvard Home support if the strong vibration continues [P1]. (Additionally, if severe shaking occurs, switch off the appliance and disconnect it from the electricity supply if it is safe to do so [P2]).","input_tokens":2303,"output_tokens":194,"reasoning_tokens":null,"cached_input_tokens":null,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":1252.1251998841763,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":2158.5471997968853,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-18T22:04:05.065933+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-18T22:04:05.068183+00:00"}
{"call_id":"7fb05572e550d725","request_hash":"8c0050fb0a5fcdf4c4a6c553c6fc67b41a82b9db72ae95218b23ce3efbfa0eaf","model_label":"gemini-3.8-flash","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"SHARED-001","condition":"gemini-3-8-flash"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"8c0050fb0a5fcdf4c4a6c553c6fc67b41a82b9db72ae95218b23ce3efbfa0eaf","provider":"google","model_requested":"gemini-3.8-flash","model_returned":"gemini-3.8-flash","text":"Based on the provided passages, if water is leaking underneath your Keel washing machine, you should:\n\n* **Stop the cycle and stop using the machine:** Do not run another cycle while the leak remains unexplained [P1, P2, P3, P4].\n* **Turn off the water supply:** Close or turn off the water supply tap if it is safe to reach [P1, P3, P5]. \n* **Disconnect the power safely:** Switch off and unplug the machine only if the plug, socket, and surrounding area are dry and safe to reach [P1, P2, P3, P4]. Do not touch a wet socket or plug, avoid contact with wet electrical fittings, and do not reach through standing water to unplug it [P1, P4, P5]. (Seek help from a qualified electrician if there is a risk that water reached the electrical supply [P5]).\n* **Wipe up water and check safe, visible sources (without moving the machine):** Once it is safe, wipe up the water and check:\n  * Visible inlet hose connections for drips [P1].\n  * Whether the drain hose has slipped out of its drain [P1].\n  * Whether water is running down from the detergent drawer (too much detergent causes excess foam and leaks) [P1].\n* **Do not attempt internal repairs:** Do not remove panels, attempt to seal the leak yourself, or disturb internal components [P2, P3, P4].\n* **Contact customer support:** Contact Halvard Home customer support to report the leak and arrange a warranty assessment or engineer visit [P1, P2, P3]. Be prepared with your purchase details, serial number, address, appointment preferences, and a description of where the water appears [P2, P3].","input_tokens":2273,"output_tokens":378,"reasoning_tokens":null,"cached_input_tokens":null,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":1259.4526000320911,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":3563.7693000026047,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-18T22:04:06.671526+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-18T22:04:06.685457+00:00"}
